 34SI cL $2001Nu01 proposed that 1193.3|g possibly populates excited 0+ state at
 34SI2cL 2133 keV. 2002En02 in {+9}Be({+35}Si,{+34}SiX|g) reaction reported an  
 34SI3cL 1193|g from 3327 level with a branching of about 13%, but 2002Mi44 set 
 34SI4cL an upper limit of 1% for such a transition in their                    
 34SI5cL Si({+34}Si,{+34}Si'|g) reaction study. 2003Iw02 observed 1193|g in coin
 34SI6cL with 3326|g, thus negating the placement of 1193 transition in parallel
 34SI7cL with 3326 transition as well as the existence of an excited 0+ level at
 34SI8cL 2133 keV                                                               
